#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192405 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "421b9396-2a7b-5c45-897a-9de5f52683de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0042ce26-8793-5690-b4ab-9f018afe979a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10459" :question/problem "The function $f(x) = \\dfrac{4}{(x-1)^2}$ is defined for $x >1.$ Find $f^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{4}{(x-1)^2}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{4}{(y-1)^2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{4}{(y-1)^{2}} \\\\ x\\cdot (y-1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =\\frac{4}{x} \\\\ \\sqrt{(y-1)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{x}} \\\\ |y-1| & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that for $y > 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n|y-1| = y-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} + 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192406 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7266d5c7-67b9-59db-b994-07dcb143af1f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Simple Rational Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9b149c51-015f-5346-9fca-8da406d0a79a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10460" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{2-x}{x+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{2-x}{x+3}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{2-y}{y+3}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2-y}{y+3} \\\\ x(y+3) & =2-y \\\\ xy+3x & =2-y \\\\ xy+y & =2-3x \\\\ y(x+1) & =2-3x \\\\ y & =\\frac{2-3x}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{2-3x}{x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192407 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Value Given the Inverse of a Rational Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f6ab6606-77ce-583a-9712-175825864612" :question/math-academy-id "e-10461" :question/problem "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{kx + 6}{x-4}, \\qquad x\\neq 4\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{4x+6}{x-2}, \\qquad x\\neq 2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny =  \\dfrac{kx + 6}{x-4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{ky+6}{y-4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{ky+6}{y-4} \\\\ x(y-4) & =ky+6 \\\\ xy-4x & =ky+6 \\\\ xy-ky & =4x+6 \\\\ y(x-k) & =4x+6 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+6}{x-k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{4x+6}{x-k}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "421b9396-2a7b-5c45-897a-9de5f52683de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62bd6a3f-2665-5667-b075-452e78b8484b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5x+2}{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555217} {:answer/id #uuid "70a3807c-efb7-50c2-856b-6caed6fe1466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+5}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555256} {:answer/id #uuid "796d30cc-8ef1-5721-aa46-8acb1556f524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+2}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555281} {:answer/id #uuid "abea9c1e-3de0-5270-839c-3aa369a4c78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5x+6}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555413} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4fd328-282d-55a2-b9f7-423cf9af6889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{2x+5}{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70a3807c-efb7-50c2-856b-6caed6fe1466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+5}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555256} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f57c79-a474-5ca6-b43c-dfe1a0e9310d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3136287b-ab52-50e3-8963-70ea96c4eb24" :question/math-academy-id "q-148432" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{2x-6}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{2x-6}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{2y-6}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{2y-6} \\\\ x(2y-6) & =5 \\\\ 2xy-6x & =5 \\\\ 2xy & =6x+5 \\\\ y & =\\frac{6x+5}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+5}{2x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "421b9396-2a7b-5c45-897a-9de5f52683de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Reciprocal Function"}] :questio