^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{8x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555122} {:answer/id #uuid "882d748e-7e50-57e5-99c6-6959f77c6e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555317} {:answer/id #uuid "a7468134-1b70-5e93-ab53-83a256b45e88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8+x}{x+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555400} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1e5163-c8eb-51ff-bd6c-d109838ee488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-8}{5x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "882d748e-7e50-57e5-99c6-6959f77c6e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555317} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d60ccb-7323-5847-8254-46df29873deb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "411f5065-9d51-51d9-906e-20eb90eb5d15" :question/math-academy-id "q-148507" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{x-8}{5x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{x-8}{5x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{y-8}{5y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{y-8}{5y+1} \\\\ -x & =\\frac{y-8}{5y+1} \\\\ -x(5y+1) & =y-8 \\\\ -5xy-x & =y-8 \\\\ 8-x & =5xy+y \\\\ 8-x & =y(5x+1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7266d5c7-67b9-59db-b994-07dcb143af1f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Simple Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "016428bb-9b2a-5acd-8baf-3acf6f1ba744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555007} {:answer/id #uuid "20e7484f-fbbe-5b08-bcac-c2785c1893e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{2x-5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555064} {:answer/id #uuid "968e8cbc-ee3b-507c-836c-108dd308cb48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5+x}{2x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555360} {:answer/id #uuid "9f87e1ab-5c04-53d3-9116-9fa836141840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+5}{2-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555385} {:answer/id #uuid "ff187826-3ec3-5529-817a-9c5e929bb4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-x}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff187826-3ec3-5529-817a-9c5e929bb4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-x}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555635} :answer-field/id #uuid "59384b78-3cc9-5dfa-a137-2e35558b2a9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de7ae964-9fce-58b0-bd1b-ba5303123396" :question/math-academy-id "q-148508" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5-2y}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5-2y}{y+1} \\\\ x(y+1) & =5-2y \\\\ xy+x & =5-2y \\\\ xy+2y & =5-x \\\\ y(x+2) & =5-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5-x}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-x}{x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Value Given the Inverse of a Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ac1e3c6-b482-5ff8-b9a9-e773f457d7b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555049} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2861d3-1422-5dd0-b377-19f88162a86e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555211} {:answer/id #uuid "73fcfb27-eaff-5647-944c-46439323073f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555262} {:answer/id #uuid "76531f62-9097-54a3-ab2b-ca46f34bbee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555269} {:answer/id #uuid "dd711d56-e65b-5d4d-8e2e-4779c583661e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd711d56-e65b-5d4d-8e2e-4779c583661e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555538} :answer-field/id #uuid "f55732d7-aca2-51a2-90ac-0f461a312d8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa405f43-aa49-5df2-9659-18d1b520e384" :question/math-academy-id "q-148537" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{7x+k}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1+3x}{7x}.$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{7x+k}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{7y+k}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{7y+k} \\\\ x(7y+k) & =1 \\\\ 7xy+kx & =1 \\\\ 7xy & =1-kx \\\\ y & =\\frac{1-kx}{7x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1-kx}{7x}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Value Given the Inverse of a Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0abf8c-85fb-551c-9ea5-437c81c3f948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555128} {:answer/id #uuid "b1856ebd-05b3-5b96-80e5-a49aeba1092f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555428} {:answer/id #uuid "b43ce641-61bc-5f97-84f4-f02b82e2005b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555436} {:answer/id #uuid "eae4f622-afce-53d0-bbc6-e7205a79fc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555576} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e23358-fa26-5ecc-beff-81359458ba1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b43ce641-61bc-5f97-84f4-f02b82e2005b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555436} :answer-field/id #uuid "81ce0f55-8715-56de-87b9-343c421ef84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bd71fc1-9e9b-5a64-b8c7-ee650f7e3c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-148539" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{3}{kx-2}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3+2x}{5x}.$ What is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{kx-2}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{ky-2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3}{ky-2} \\\\ x(ky-2) & =3 \\\\ kxy-2x & =3 \\\\ kxy & =3+2x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3+2x}{kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3+2x}{kx}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Value Given the Inverse of a Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0827d445-54bb-5a4c-8341-aefe90394569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555014} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2e54fc-a95a-5356-b970-579dea53d954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555215} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c4dd6b-e1c5-52bc-9780-636b2e616133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555431} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d4c450-85ec-5882-a428-b063c2aa7bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555438} {:answer/id #uuid "f5842b48-e760-5215-af2b-61005182e37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7d4c450-85ec-5882-a428-b063c2aa7bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555438} :answer-field/id #uuid "16bcada1-2264-5573-b603-5074361a0f9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "754f4c4b-11dc-5f96-9fa9-3c28fe7e8a39" :question/math-academy-id "q-148584" :question/problem "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2x+k}{x-1},\\,x\\ne 1\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-8}{x-2},\\,x\\ne 2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2x+k}{x-1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2y+k}{y-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2y+k}{y-1} \\\\ x(y-1) & =2y+k \\\\ xy-x & =2y+k \\\\ xy-2y & =x+k \\\\ y(x-2) & =x+k \\\\ y & =\\frac{x+k}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+k}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Value Given the Inverse of a Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3b2196-8607-5fc9-a852-5f2997daec12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555213} {:answer/id #uuid "8372edf8-2062-5f14-bc0d-326bb8851d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555302} {:answer/id #uuid "b355850a-c9b6-5f69-9884-3502d004fb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555434} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcd4de5-18ea-5e4c-9b72-a2b6952a3a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555452} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6b8691-1372-5998-8571-69302ac6ed6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e3b2196-8607-5fc9-a852-5f2997daec12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555213} :answer-field/id #uuid "d49e749e-69c5-5c58-ab0b-3f74366a64e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "36115cd9-9382-506b-9404-8a68bbaccae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-148588" :question/problem "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-kx}{x+1},\\,x\\ne -1\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3-x}{x+4},\\,x\\ne -4.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3-kx}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3-ky}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3-ky}{y+1} \\\\ x(y+1) & =3-ky \\\\ xy+x & =3-ky \\\\ xy+ky & =3-x \\\\ y(x+k) & =3-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3-x}{x+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3-x}{x+k}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "421b9396-2a7b-5c45-897a-9de5f52683de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bae21e18-9aeb-5d48-b0dd-753057a50a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x-2}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bae21e18-9aeb-5d48-b0dd-753057a50a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x-2}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555445} :answer-field/id #uuid "e97ae974-ae89-5e50-835c-a14289debe35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "306d067e-7a9d-57e7-9fd1-1469fa53a6b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-276631" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{7-5x}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{7-5x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{7-5y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{7-5y} \\\\ x(7-5y) & =2 \\\\ 7x-5xy & =2 \\\\ -5xy & =2-7x \\\\ 5xy & =7x-2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x-2}{5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{7x-2}{5x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "421b9396-2a7b-5c45-897a-9de5f52683de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47bbaa97-6413-54a1-9502-e9fda4b11eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5-2x}{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47bbaa97-6413-54a1-9502-e9fda4b11eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5-2x}{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555153} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa31e955-275b-5fef-861b-ebf469837989" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a700c45d-e998-5eef-9aa2-096588d12ebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-276634" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{6x+2}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{6x+2}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{6y+2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{6y+2} \\\\ x(6y+2) & =5 \\\\ 6xy+2x & =5 \\\\ 6xy & =5-2x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5-2x}{6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{6x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "421b9396-2a7b-5c45-897a-9de5f52683de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cecda5c-102e-5a0a-a6ab-c0bc483ddb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cecda5c-102e-5a0a-a6ab-c0bc483ddb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555023} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5552c58-f49c-529a-9760-0d2cd4c8e4de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ea6de0b-579b-595d-b4da-dc4ce1abfbcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-276645" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{(4x+7)^{2}}$ is defined for $x>-\\frac{7}{4}.$ Find ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{(4x+7)^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{(4y+7)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{(4y+7)^{2}} \\\\ x(4y+7)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (4y+7)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\sqrt{(4y+7)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{x}} \\\\ |4y+7| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 4y+7 & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 4y & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-7 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that for $y>-\\frac{7}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n|4y+7|=4y+7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7266d5c7-67b9-59db-b994-07dcb143af1f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Simple Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3fcfb0f-1f3c-52ea-bf6f-630b1f5d1f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3fcfb0f-1f3c-52ea-bf6f-630b1f5d1f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555503} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c890417-6b3f-5bb6-b26f-482f2ab4cfca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a45b39d-afe3-5e4b-83e0-4037874d7882" :question/math-academy-id "q-276777" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{2x-5}{x-4}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2x-5}{x-4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{2y-5}{y-4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{2y-5}{y-4} \\\\ -x & =\\frac{2y-5}{y-4} \\\\ -x(y-4) & =2y-5 \\\\ -xy+4x & =2y-5 \\\\ 4x+5 & =xy+2y \\\\ 4x+5 & =y(x+2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+5}{x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dcedd9d0-f87c-58b2-9ef1-c9fa0ef2e5c1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining an Unknown Value Given the Inverse of a Rational Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0b92cfe-c4f6-5406-8f8b-26ffd1c4ea92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b92cfe-c4f6-5406-8f8b-26ffd1c4ea92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555425} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b18f9b-8d04-502e-a1b1-ced120e8f787" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e33bcefe-71b8-5e01-9202-e30bde07e783" :question/math-academy-id "q-276781" :question/problem "The function $f(x)=\\frac{3k}{6+4x}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9-6x}{4x}.$ What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3k}{6+4x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3k}{6+4y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3k}{6+4y} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3k}{6+4y} \\\\ x(6+4y) & =3k \\\\ 6x+4xy & =3k \\\\ 4xy & =3k-6x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3k-6x}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3k-6x}{4x}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=3.$"}]}
